# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Heavy, regenerable artifacts (never in Git)
# (cache features live in cache/ and are *.npz, so no broad "features/" pattern --
#  that would also ignore the src/luq/features/ source code.)
hf_cache/
saved_outputs/
cache/
results/
logs/
*.pt
*.npz

# Scheduler job logs: PBS/Slurm write <jobname>.o<jobid> / .e<jobid> stdout+stderr
# into the submit dir. Regenerable console output, never source -- ignore them.
*.o[0-9]*
*.e[0-9]*

# Transient scheduler bookkeeping written by the job-watcher shell loops: bare lists of PBS job
# IDs, and a zero-byte "fleet launched" sentinel. Five of these were committed by accident and
# untracked on 2026-08-14. The job IDs are long dead and document nothing reproducible.
.luq_*
.seg_fleet_launched

# Secrets
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store

# PBS job logs (persistent by design -- see pbs/topk_prior_one_eval.pbs -- but not artifacts to track)
logs/

# A worktree's cache is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's cache, so the existing 'cache/'
# pattern (which matches directories) never matched it and it sat untracked forever. A permanently
# dirty 'git status' is not cosmetic here: the untracked-file sweep relies on it.
cache

# `results` is a SYMLINK to ../results, i.e. to a directory outside this repository, where the
# result files are version-controlled separately (they are not part of the published artifact).
# The code keeps reading and writing `results/...` exactly as before, because this path still
# resolves -- that is the entire point of the symlink, and it is why no driver, PBS script or glob
# needed changing. Same trailing-slash trap as `cache` above: the 'results/' pattern on line 12
# matches a DIRECTORY and does NOT match this symlink, so the bare form is required or the tree
# reads permanently dirty and the untracked-file sweep stops working.
results

# ---- WORKING NOTES DO NOT BELONG IN THE SUBMITTED REPO ----
# This repo is the submitted artifact and should read as a record of what was actually RUN.
# Cluster hand-overs, session notes and "how to find your bearings" explainers are working notes:
# they are kept outside this repository, alongside the planning documents. Pre-registrations and
# analysis scripts are NOT in this class -- they are part of the record and stay tracked here.
*_BRIEF_*.md
DOC_BRIEF*.md
DOC_INSTRUCTIONS.md
AGENT_*.md
*_HANDOVER*.md

# Editor / tooling scratch directories and worktrees. A 42MB unlabelled records duplicate was found
# in one of these on 2026-08-11, untracked but NOT ignored, so a `git add -A` would have swept it
# into the submitted artifact.
.claude/
